PART 6: DEPENDENCY ARRAY
================================================================================

CASE 1: NO CHANGING REACTIVE DEPENDENCY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

useEffect(() => {

  loadInitialData()

}, [])


Conceptually:

Component appears
      ↓
Effect establishes initial synchronization


================================================================================
IMPORTANT CORRECTION
================================================================================

Do NOT memorize:

[] =
EXACTLY ONCE FOREVER


A better meaning is:

[] =
THIS EFFECT USES NO CHANGING REACTIVE DEPENDENCIES


Development Strict Mode may intentionally perform:

Setup
 ↓
Cleanup
 ↓
Setup


to help expose broken Effect logic.


Therefore Effects should be written safely rather than relying on the idea
that setup can physically happen only once.


================================================================================
CASE 2: RESOURCE DEPENDS ON userId
================================================================================

useEffect(() => {

  loadUser(
    userId
  )

}, [
  userId
])


Flow:

userId = 10
      ↓
Fetch User 10


Later:

userId = 20
      ↓
Cleanup old request
      ↓
Fetch User 20


================================================================================
CASE 3: MULTIPLE DEPENDENCIES
================================================================================

useEffect(() => {

  loadProducts(
    category,
    searchText
  )

}, [
  category,
  searchText
])


Effect synchronizes when:

category

or:

searchText


changes.


================================================================================
DEPENDENCY TABLE
================================================================================

+------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| DEPENDENCIES           | BEHAVIOR                                    |
+------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| omitted                | Runs after every relevant committed render  |
| []                     | No changing reactive dependencies           |
| [userId]               | Reacts to userId                            |
| [category, searchText] | Reacts to either dependency                 |
+------------------------+---------------------------------------------+


