PART 7: ERROR HANDLING
================================================================================

NETWORK ERROR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:

Network unavailable


Then:

fetch()


may reject.


The catch block handles:

catch (error) {

  ...
}


================================================================================
HTTP ERROR
================================================================================

Example:

404

500

503


Important:

fetch() does NOT automatically reject merely because the server returned an
HTTP error status.


Therefore:

if (!response.ok) {

  throw new Error(
    `Request failed with status ${response.status}`
  )
}


================================================================================
ERROR FLOW
================================================================================

fetch()
  ↓
Something fails
  ↓
catch
  ↓
AbortError?
 /        \
YES       NO
↓          ↓
Ignore    setError()
            ↓
          UI Error


================================================================================
ERROR UI
================================================================================

if (error) {

  return (

    <p role="alert">

      Error:
      {' '}
      {error}

    </p>

  )
}


This gives the user actual feedback instead of leaving:

Loading...


forever.


