PART 8: REQUEST CANCELLATION AND RACE CONDITIONS
================================================================================

WHY USE AbortController?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Consider:

userId = 10


Request A:

GET /api/users/10


Before it finishes:

userId = 20


Request B:

GET /api/users/20


Suppose:

Request B finishes FIRST.


UI:

User 20


Then Request A finishes later.


Without protection:

UI could incorrectly become:

User 10


This is a:

RACE CONDITION


================================================================================
WITH CLEANUP
================================================================================

useEffect(() => {

  const controller =
    new AbortController()


  fetch(
    `/api/users/${userId}`,
    {
      signal:
        controller.signal
    }
  )


  return () => {

    controller.abort()

  }

}, [
  userId
])


Flow:

Request User 10
      ↓
userId changes
      ↓
Cleanup
      ↓
Abort User 10 Request
      ↓
Request User 20
      ↓
Latest Data Wins


================================================================================
WHY IGNORE AbortError?
================================================================================

Cancellation is expected behavior.


It does NOT mean:

"The server failed."


Therefore:

catch (error) {

  if (
    error.name ===
    'AbortError'
  ) {

    return
  }


  setError(
    error.message
  )
}


